<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madan Singh of Jhalawar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1845</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madan Singh was the first ruler of Jhalawar State in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputana">Rajputana</a>, reigning from 1838 to 1845. He was the grandson of Zalim Singh, the powerful regent of Kota, and the British created Jhalawar for him out of Kota territory to end the long rivalry between the regent's family and the Kota rulers. He took the title Maharaj Rana.</p></div>
